cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AURORA IDE — the SAPHO platform IDE"
message: "If you use AURORA or the SAPHO platform in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  # Luciano Manhães de Andrade Filho — advisor (orientador).
  - given-names: "Luciano M. de A."
    family-names: "Filho"
    affiliation: "NIPS-CERN — Universidade Federal de Juiz de Fora"
  # Chrysthofer Arthur Amaro Afonso — undergraduate (graduando).
  - given-names: "Chrysthofer A. A."
    family-names: "Afonso"
    affiliation: "NIPS-CERN — Universidade Federal de Juiz de Fora"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nipscernlab/aurora"
url: "https://www.nipscern.com"
abstract: >-
  AURORA is the integrated development environment for the SAPHO platform: it
  unifies writing C±, assembling, synthesising Verilog, simulating, viewing
  waveforms, and inspecting RTL behind one interface built on Electron and Monaco.
keywords:
  - EDA
  - HDL
  - Verilog
  - soft-processor
  - FPGA
  - Electron
  - Monaco
# The NIPS-CERN Licence 1.1 has no SPDX identifier, so CFF's `license:` key
# (SPDX-only) cannot carry it. `license-url` is the spec's escape hatch.
license-url: "https://github.com/nipscernlab/aurora/blob/main/LICENSE"
# Both lines are rewritten by release-please on every release (the file is
# listed under `extra-files` in release-please-config.json). Editing them by
# hand is how they drifted before: the version tracked the releases and the
# date stayed at the day someone last remembered it.
version: 6.13.0 # x-release-please-version
date-released: "2026-09-02" # x-release-please-date
